  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the lines $\\mathrm{L}_1: \\mathrm{x}-1=\\mathrm{y}-2=\\mathrm{z}$ and $\\mathrm{L}_2: \\mathrm{x}-2=\\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{z}-1$. Let the feet of the perpendiculars from the point $\\mathrm{P}(5,1,-3)$ on the lines $\\mathrm{L}_1$ and $\\mathrm{L}_2$ be $Q$ and $R$ respectively. If the area of the triangle PQR is A , then $4 \\mathrm{~A}^2$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZOHa2",
      "text": "139",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
